cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CLEETS-CHAT, please cite it as below, and cite the CLEETS-KG data set separately (see README)."
title: "CLEETS-CHAT: Cited and Hallucination-Free AI with Traceability"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Naeima/cleets-chat"
url: "https://naeima.github.io/cleets-chat/"
abstract: >-
  Question answering over the CLEETS knowledge graphs of electric-vehicle adoption in Wales.
  Answers are composed from retrieved RDF statements and deterministic calculations, cite their
  source datasets, separate observed from predicted values, and explain how each prediction type
  of the companion paper was generated. Includes a Dash dashboard, a static GitHub Pages build
  that runs the same Python code in the browser, custom dataset extraction with map plotting and
  CSV download, and stakeholder scoring of answers.
authors:
